{"id": "EUVD-2026-101132", "enisaUuid": "fc2f0e4e-c705-363d-a173-c7abacd49bc4", "description": "ELFIO through 3.12 contains a NULL pointer dereference vulnerability in relocation_section_accessor get_entry() that allows attackers to crash applications via an unvalidated sh_link index. Attackers can supply a crafted ELF file whose SHT_REL or SHT_RELA section has a dangling sh_link, causing find_hash_section() to dereference null and deny service.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T15:01:25", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T01:27:15", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/elfio-relocation-get-entry-null-deref", "https://github.com/serge1/ELFIO/blob/8ae6cec5d60495822ecd57d736f66149da9b1830/elfio/elfio_relocation.hpp#L142", "https://github.com/serge1/ELFIO", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/elfio-through-3.12-null-pointer-dereference-via-relocation-section-accessor-get-entry"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-110659", "GHSA-78jh-26cf-3958"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "e62d6385-33d6-3d8b-9e5c-09869ca56894", "product": {"name": "ELFIO", "vendor": {"name": "serge1"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22643.12"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0888c87c-6a6c-3d4c-9ef1-fcaaeb865ff9", "vendor": {"name": "serge1"}}], "isExploited": false}